+`/v1/account_disconnect`
+------------------------
+
+This endpoint disconnects every client logged into an account (always-on clients included) and turns always-on off for it, so that an account disabled in an external account system leaves at once and doesn't come back at a restart. The account itself is kept. The request is a JSON object with fields:
+
+* `accountName`: string, name of the account
+* `reason`: string, optional: the quit message
+
+The response is a JSON object with fields:
+
+* `success`: whether the request was valid (also when nobody was connected)
+* `clients`: the number of clients disconnected
+* `errorCode`: string, optional, machine-readable description of the error. Possible values include: `ACCOUNT_DOES_NOT_EXIST` (not a valid account name).
+
 `/v1/rehash`
 ------------
 
